			<performanceExamScore>45</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Indecision is just another form of weakness, and Chong-su refuses to entertain it. They make the call, moves forward, and never looks back - because in the brutal reality of war, second-guessing gets people killed. Chong-su doesn&apos;t trust high-level strategies or overcomplicated maneuvers. They believe victory comes from direct control, from positioning, from knowing exactly what&apos;s happening in the fight - not from a distant command center. &quot;You want to win? Get your hands dirty and see the fight yourself.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees hesitation as lethal. Makes the call, never looks back. Hard charger.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
