			<personalityDescription>Subtlety and patience have never been Anne&apos;s strengths. She speaks before thinking, acts before planning, and never apologizes for either. If boldness is a virtue, then she considers herself a saint. Anne doesn&apos;t stop - ever. Even when reason, exhaustion, or sheer survival say she should walk away, she grits her teeth and keeps going. She&apos;ll finish what she started, even if it kills her. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 32%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- No patience, no filter, no regrets. Speaks and acts before thinking. Owns it.&lt;br&gt;- Pushes past sense and safety. Finishes what they start, or dies trying.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
