			<personalityDescription>If it&apos;s crazy, reckless, or just plain stupid, Harold is probably already doing it. He doesn&apos;t just flirt with danger - he buys it a drink and takes it for a ride, laughing in the face of common sense all the way. Trusting Harold is a mistake most people only make once. He weaves a careful web of half-truths and false assurances, making it nearly impossible to tell where his real motives lie - until he&apos;s already gotten what he wanted. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Chases danger for fun. Dares what others dismiss. Laughs off rules.&lt;br&gt;- Smiles like a friend, schemes like an enemy. Don&apos;t turn your back.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
