			<performanceExamScore>45</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Patience has never been Lewis&apos;s strong suit. He leans forward in every briefing, itching to get moving, his restless energy practically vibrating through the room. Sitting still isn&apos;t an option - he lives for action, for motion, for doing something. &quot;We&apos;ve got enough fuel for the next campaign, Lewis.&quot; He scoffs. &quot;Assuming we don&apos;t get shorted on the next shipment, or the price spikes, or some idiot burns through half our reserves on a miscalculation.&quot; If there&apos;s a way for things to go wrong, Lewis&apos;s already considered it twice. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Can&apos;t sit still - lives for the green light.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
