			<personalityDescription>If there&apos;s a risk to take, Scanlon is already halfway through it. He thrives on danger, seeing every challenge as an opportunity and every battle as an adventure waiting to unfold. Safe choices are for lesser warriors. Scanlon doesn&apos;t explain himself because he knows that if people knew the truth, they&apos;d never trust him again. His motives are buried under layers of necessity and survival. &quot;You don&apos;t need to know why I&apos;m doing this. You just need to decide if you&apos;re coming with me or not.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Risks draw them in. Sees combat as challenge, not threat.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
