			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Michele could probably win more fights if she didn&apos;t spend so much time starting them. Whether it&apos;s trash-talking over comms or throwing the first punch in a negotiation, she seems to believe the best way to solve a problem is by making it someone else&apos;s problem. Fist first. Small talk? Useless. Second-guessing orders? Infuriating. Michele&apos;s tolerance for anything that slows her down is nonexistent. She&apos;s not always outright angry, but the scowl, the sharp tone, and the way she glares say more than words ever could. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Starts problems just to end them violently. First to swing, last to think.&lt;br&gt;- Mood? Permanent scowl. Voice? Razor-edged.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
