			<personalityDescription>There&apos;s no middle ground with Marx - everything is turned up to eleven. He doesn&apos;t just prepare; he over-prepares. He doesn&apos;t just act; he goes all out. If there&apos;s a way to dial it back, he hasn&apos;t found it yet. Marx sees people as tools - useful until they&apos;re not. He takes what he needs, wrings every ounce of value out of those around him, and discards them the moment they become dead weight. Loyalty and morality are just obstacles to be overcome. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Cranks every dial to max. No balance, no brakes.&lt;br&gt;- Treats people like tools - breaks them, bins them, moves on.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
