			<performanceExamScore>51</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Marjorie makes decisions in the heat of the moment, trusting gut instinct over careful planning. Whether in battle or conversation, she acts first and thinks later - sometimes to great effect, sometimes to great regret. Marjorie can&apos;t stand clutter, grime, or grease stains, which makes her a constant presence in the repair bay. Whether she&apos;s scrubbing someone else&apos;s tools or wiping down DropShip corridors, she&apos;s always cleaning something - and somehow, that relentless energy keeps the whole operation running smoother. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Gut-driven. Acts fast, sometimes smart - sometimes not. Unpredictable asset.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
