			<performanceExamScore>49</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Callum plays by his own rules, which change depending on what benefits him most. He&apos;s not a villain - he just doesn&apos;t see the point in letting things like loyalty or honesty get in the way of a good deal or an easy victory. Before every battle, Callum insists on running a final check. Formation assignments? Confirmed. Backup comms? Verified. Extraction routes? Plotted and re-plotted. &quot;The battlefield is messy enough,&quot; he mutters. &quot;No reason we have to be.&quot; The others may roll their eyes, but when things go wrong, his plans are why they make it out alive. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Rules bend around them - ethics don&apos;t apply.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
