			<personalityDescription>Once Anwa makes up his mind, that&apos;s the end of the discussion. Plans don&apos;t change, orders don&apos;t get questioned, and he sure as hell isn&apos;t going to admit being  wrong - not now, not ever. Anwa doesn&apos;t waste time on altruism - every deal, every alliance, every action is about securing his own advantage. If helping someone else happens to benefit him too, all the better - but if it doesn&apos;t, he won&apos;t waste a second thought on them. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Decisions are final. Won&apos;t revisit, revise, or admit error.&lt;br&gt;- Won&apos;t lift a finger unless it pays out.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
