			<personalityDescription>Caution is for the slow and the dead, and Ijo refuses to be either. He rushes headlong into danger, making split-second decisions that could be called bravery - or  sheer madness. One way or another, Ijo never stands still. Ijo doesn&apos;t deal in half-truths or carefully worded pleasantries. He calls things exactly as he sees them, no matter how uncomfortable it makes people - because, to him, honesty is more valuable than diplomacy. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Rejects caution. Speed over safety. Bravery or recklessness - depends on the day.&lt;br&gt;- Says the thing everyone else avoids - loud, clear, and on purpose.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
