			<personalityDescription>To Young-Shil, control isn&apos;t a preference - it&apos;s a necessity. She dictates every move, barks orders without question, and refuses to tolerate disobedience. In her world, authority isn&apos;t earned - it&apos;s enforced. When others falter, Young-Shil keeps moving. She refuses to accept failure as an option, pushing forward with relentless determination, no matter how long it takes to succeed. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Enforces authority, not leadership. Obedience expected, not requested.&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t accept failure. Grinds forward no matter the toll.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
