			<personalityDescription>Marie doesn&apos;t measure risk the way others do. Where they see danger, she sees duty; where others hesitate, she moves forward. Not because she doesn&apos;t feel fear, but because she refuses to let it define her. Marie doesn&apos;t care about honor or fair fights - only winning. She exploits weaknesses, sacrifices pawns when necessary, and always fights on her terms. If the enemy expects a straight fight, they&apos;ve already lost. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees duty, not danger. Fear present - but doesn&apos;t get a say.&lt;br&gt;- No honor, no hesitation - just results.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
