			<personalityDescription>Indecision is just another form of weakness, and Berit refuses to entertain it. She makes the call, moves forward, and never looks back - because in the brutal reality of war, second-guessing gets people killed. Berit doesn&apos;t just hear callsigns - she remembers them. Every hero, every ace, every fallen comrade - she keeps a mental log. &quot;Stormbringer? Yeah, I fought against them once. Tough bastard. Still out there?&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees hesitation as lethal. Makes the call, never looks back. Hard charger.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
