			<performanceExamScore>48</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>To Wildemar, control isn&apos;t a preference - it&apos;s a necessity. They dictate every move, barks orders without question, and refuses to tolerate disobedience. In their world, authority isn&apos;t earned - it&apos;s enforced. Wildemar knows that if they ever let things go silent, the memories will start creeping back in. The people who aren&apos;t here anymore, the things they should have done differently. So the music stays on - always. &quot;The second the music stops, that&apos;s when it gets bad. And I don&apos;t plan on letting it stop.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Enforces authority, not leadership. Obedience expected, not requested.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
