			<personalityDescription>Agreni doesn&apos;t seek victory - he seeks peace. Every fight, every battle, every loss only reinforces his conviction that the real war isn&apos;t against an enemy, but against the need to fight at all. Agreni never stops - because stopping means thinking, and thinking means facing the ghosts that haunt him. He fights, trains, and pushes himself beyond exhaustion, running from a past that never quite lets him rest. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Fighting for peace, not conquest. Enemy is the cycle of war itself.&lt;br&gt;- Pushing past exhaustion to outrun something deeper. Momentum masks pain.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
