			<personalityDescription>Once Lee-Suan sets her sights on something, there&apos;s no shaking her. She&apos;ll keep coming, keep working, and keep fighting long after others would have given up, proving that sheer force of will can sometimes be the most dangerous weapon of all. Lee-Suan has seen teammates disappear, heard allies fall silent, felt the weight of being the last one alive. She doesn&apos;t fear isolation itself - she fears what it means. &quot;The second you&apos;re alone? That&apos;s when you know it&apos;s over.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Once committed, won&apos;t let go. Willpower becomes weapon.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
