			<personalityDescription>Revekka never stops - because stopping means thinking, and thinking means facing the ghosts that haunt her. She fights, trains, and pushes herself beyond exhaustion, running from a past that never quite lets her rest. Revekka fights hard, fast, aggressive - but it never feels natural. There&apos;s a hesitation in her movements, a disconnect between body and instinct, like she&apos;s piloting herself instead of simply existing. &quot;I move because standing still feels worse.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Pushing past exhaustion to outrun something deeper. Momentum masks pain.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
