			<personalityDescription>Even in the heat of war, Mitchell never loses sight of the people fighting beside him. Whether it&apos;s sharing supplies, covering for a comrade&apos;s mistake, or simply checking in, he proves that true leadership starts with empathy. Whether it&apos;s a well-worn multitool, an old pocket watch, or a scrap of a long faded photo, Mitchell&apos;s always carrying something familiar. &quot;You gotta have something of your own in a job like this,&quot; he says. No one knows where he got it, but they know he&apos;d notice immediately if it ever went missing. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Leads with empathy. The kind we need more of.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
