			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Once, Gerhardt might have wanted more, but now? He&apos;s seen too many people claw their way to the top only to die just like everyone else. Ambition is just another word for desperation, and Gerhardt has long since stopped caring. There&apos;s not much softness in the military life - just rations, burnt coffee, and the bitter taste of war. But gum? Gum reminds Gerhardt that there used to be shops, vendors, normalcy. Every time he unwraps a fresh stick, he pretends, for just a second, that he&apos;s somewhere else. Somewhere safer. Somewhere that still exists. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Burned out or just gave up - either way, not climbing.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
