			<personalityDescription>Safiyya could probably win more fights if she didn&apos;t spend so much time starting them. Whether it&apos;s trash-talking over comms or throwing the first punch in a negotiation, she seems to believe the best way to solve a problem is by making it someone else&apos;s problem. Fist first. Safiyya doesn&apos;t rush - she refines. Every plan, every shot, every move is calculated and practiced until it&apos;s second nature. She believes that mastery comes from discipline, and discipline comes from doing the work no one else is willing to. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 61%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Starts problems just to end them violently. First to swing, last to think.&lt;br&gt;- Repetition breeds mastery. Refines until perfection is habit.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
