			<reasoning>14</reasoning>
			<performanceExamScore>60</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Some people make friends. Phoenix makes enemies - and seems to prefer it that way. Whether through biting sarcasm or outright aggression, he turns every interaction into a fight waiting to happen, and frankly, Phoenix wouldn&apos;t have it any other way. Phoenix pushes up his glasses like it&apos;ll make the world clearer, like it&apos;ll help him understand why he&apos;s still alive when so many aren&apos;t. He sees every mistake, every miscalculation, every doomed maneuver before it happens - but no one ever listens in time. He keeps adjusting his glasses, keeps trying to see better - but it doesn&apos;t change a damn thing. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Makes enemies on purpose. Finds comfort in conflict, not camaraderie.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
