			<personalityDescription>While he doesn&apos;t seek attention, Jamie notices everything. He listens more than he speaks, analyzes before he acts, and values deep conversations over shallow chatter. His quiet nature makes his words all the more impactful when he chooses to share them. Jamie&apos;s words jump between cold, clinical detachment and erratic, almost manic tangents. One second, he&apos;s reciting enemy force composition like a machine, and the next, he&apos;s muttering &quot;Bad luck always comes in threes. It&apos;s always threes.&quot; His squad pretends not to notice. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Quiet type. Won&apos;t lead the toast, but will notice who&apos;s missing.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
