			<personalityDescription>Mary has survived things that should have killed her - more than once. No matter how many times she gets knocked down, she just keeps getting back up, proving that sometimes, sheer refusal to die is a strategy all its own. Mary doesn&apos;t just avoid conflict - she redirects it. A well-placed phrase, a subtle shift in tone, or a carefully chosen silence can turn an argument into an opportunity, ensuring that things go her way without force. </personalityDescription>
