			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>No matter what gets thrown at them, Wu-sheng bounces back. Whether it&apos;s a brutal loss, a catastrophic failure, or a battlefield injury, they refuse to let anything break them. Wu-sheng knows war has always been brutal, but they can&apos;t help but feel that something was different back then. Fights were personal, weapons required craftsmanship, and victory was skill, not just tech superiority. They wonder if warriors of the past would laugh at how detached war has become - or pity them for how much worse it&apos;s gotten. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Takes the hit, gets back up. Nothing breaks them for long.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
