			<personalityDescription>To Genevieve, control isn&apos;t about leadership - it&apos;s about domination. She micromanages, manipulates, and enforces her will through intimidation or force. If someone steps out of line, they&apos;ll regret it. Most people aren&apos;t worth Genevieve&apos;s attention - at least, that&apos;s how she sees it. Whether it&apos;s new recruits, subordinates, or anyone beneath her notice, she brushes them aside with a look of boredom and a dismissive wave. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Leads through domination. Controls through fear, force, or pressure.&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t even look back when leaving someone behind - already onto the next thing.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
