			<performanceExamScore>51</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Once Jae-hoon makes up their mind, that&apos;s the end of the discussion. Plans don&apos;t change, orders don&apos;t get questioned, and they sure as hell aren&apos;t going to admit being  wrong - not now, not ever. Jae-hoon pushes up their glasses like it&apos;ll make the world clearer, like it&apos;ll help them understand why they&apos;re still alive when so many aren&apos;t. They see every mistake, every miscalculation, every doomed maneuver before it happens - but no one ever listens in time. They keep adjusting their glasses, keep trying to see better - but it doesn&apos;t change a damn thing. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Decisions are final. Won&apos;t revisit, revise, or admit error.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
