			<personalityDescription>Daniel notices the details others miss - the flicker of movement in the distance, the shift in tone during negotiations. They stay sharp, ready to act at a moment&apos;s notice, because the one time they aren&apos;t prepared might be the last. Daniel doesn&apos;t see narrow escapes as luck - they see them as confirmation. Every bullet that whizzes past, every enemy that fails to land a hit just fuels their belief that they&apos;re invincible. &quot;You see that? Didn&apos;t even graze me. Like I said, they can&apos;t hit me.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Catches what others miss. Operates on constant edge-readiness.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
