			<performanceExamScore>48</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>There&apos;s a fine line between bravery and recklessness, but Joyce doesn&apos;t care. She leaps before she looks, convinced that if no one else dares to try, it just means she&apos;s the only one bold enough to succeed. Joyce cracks emotionless jokes because if she stopped to process everything, it might actually get to her. It&apos;s easier to act like it&apos;s all just a mildly inconvenient joke than admit just how close they all are to dying at any given moment. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Leaps before thinking. Believes boldness is its own justification.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
