			<personalityDescription>Every word Artie speaks is calculated. He twists the truth, plays people against each other, and makespretends to care just enough to gain trust before using it to his advantage. If someone thinks he&apos;s being sincere, they&apos;re already his next victim. Artie used to talk faster, used to joke, used to care more. Now, every word is deliberate, like he&apos;s trying not to waste them. He&apos;s seen too many people speak their last words before they even knew they&apos;d die. So now, he speaks like he&apos;s making sure every sentence matters. Because someday, he won&apos;t get another one. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Plays people like cards - gets close, gains trust, exploits it fast.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
