			<personalityDescription>Fear died a long time ago for Toni. He walks through hell with a steady hand, not because he doesn&apos;t understand the danger, but because he refuses to let it matter. If death comes, Toni will meet it head-on. Toni doesn&apos;t just dream - he plans. Every action he takes is calculated to move him forward, and he doesn&apos;t get distracted by short-term setbacks or fleeting opportunities. If he wants something, he&apos;ll get it, one way or another. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Fear is dead weight. Walks into hell like it&apos;s routine. Faces death eye-to-eye.&lt;br&gt;- Plans every step. Ignores setbacks - only progress matters.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
