			<personalityDescription>Luke never lets the truth get in the way of a good opportunity. Whether he&apos;s bluffing, sweet-talking, or outright fabricating, he always makes sure his version of reality is the one people believe. Whether it&apos;s a well-worn multitool, an old pocket watch, or a scrap of a long faded photo, Luke&apos;s always carrying something familiar. &quot;You gotta have something of your own in a job like this,&quot; he says. No one knows where he got it, but they know he&apos;d notice immediately if it ever went missing. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Reality is whatever they say it is - until it isn&apos;t.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
