			<personalityDescription>Sami has a way of seeing things that others miss. Whether it&apos;s reading people, predicting enemy movements, or understanding complex situations, his sharp mind and keen perception give him an edge in any encounter. Sami hands out nicknames like candy. It&apos;s easier than remembering real names - because real names come with memories. With losses. With faces he&apos;d rather not picture when he tries to sleep. As long as they&apos;re &apos;Deadeye&apos; or &apos;Hellhound&apos; or &apos;Bulldozer&apos;, he doesn&apos;t have to think about how many real names he&apos;s already forgotten. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees the field like a map - knows where it&apos;s going before it moves.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
