			<personalityDescription>Some call it persistence, others call it sheer stubbornness - Karina just calls it doing what needs to be done. She doesn&apos;t waste time complaining or doubting; she simply pushes forward until the job is finished. Karina always seems like she&apos;s one bad moment away from snapping. Whether it&apos;s a broken piece of gear, a slow-witted subordinate, or just a long day, her irritation simmers just beneath the surface, waiting for an excuse to boil over. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Quiet, relentless persistence. Gets it done or dies trying.&lt;br&gt;- Complains the whole op. Still finishes first.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
