			<performanceExamScore>49</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Merci says exactly what&apos;s on her mind, with no concern for sugarcoating or social niceties. If the truth is harsh, so be it - she sees no point in dressing it up. Merci insists on addressing even her closest comrades as &quot;Lieutenant,&quot; &quot;Sergeant,&quot; or &quot;esteemed colleague.&quot; No one knows if it&apos;s a quirk, a joke, or if she actually thinks they&apos;re all attending a formal gala instead of wading through battlefield wreckage. Either way, it makes war sound bizarrely polite. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t mince words - just carves straight to the bone.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
