			<performanceExamScore>47</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Robin puts in the work, no matter how long it takes. Whether it&apos;s maintaining his combat unit, planning battle strategies, or honing his skills, he refuses to cut corners - because in his mind, effort is what separates the competent from the dead. Robin doesn&apos;t fight just to win; he fights the right way. He has rules, a code, a line he won&apos;t cross - even if it would make things easier. &quot;Honor matters,&quot; he says. &quot;Without it, we&apos;re just killers in metal coffins.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Puts in the hours. Refuses shortcuts - effort equals survival.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
