			<personalityDescription>Caution is for the slow and the dead, and Chantal refuses to be either. She rushes headlong into danger, making split-second decisions that could be called bravery - or  sheer madness. One way or another, Chantal never stands still. Chantal doesn&apos;t stop - ever. Even when reason, exhaustion, or sheer survival say she should walk away, she grits her teeth and keeps going. She&apos;ll finish what she started, even if it kills her. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 59%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Rejects caution. Speed over safety. Bravery or recklessness - depends on the day.&lt;br&gt;- Pushes past sense and safety. Finishes what they start, or dies trying.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
