			<personalityDescription>Carl isn&apos;t just careful - he&apos;s possessive. He stashes supplies, claims the best loot before anyone else, and resists sharing even when he has more than enough. If someone wants something from him, they&apos;d better be ready to trade big. Carl doesn&apos;t need dramatic omens - he picks up on subtle ones. A light flickering? A bad sign. A sudden chill in the air? Something&apos;s coming. He doesn&apos;t always say what he expects to happen, but the way he reacts makes it clear - he believes something will. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 37%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- First to the salvage, last to offer help. Everything&apos;s a personal stockpile.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
