			<personalityDescription>Diane never plays fair - she plays to win. Every promise, every alliance, every deal is just another tool in her arsenal, and she always ensures she comes out ahead. Diane doesn&apos;t flinch because she&apos;s nervous - she flinches because too many times, a hand on her arm was followed by a knife, a grip on her shoulder by a strike. She&apos;s learned that even friendly touches can turn deadly in an instant. &quot;Every time someone&apos;s grabbed me without warning, something bad followed. You expect me to just forget that?&quot; </personalityDescription>
