			<personalityDescription>Alan doesn&apos;t just react to situations - he creates them. He manipulates events from behind the scenes, setting traps, forcing hands, and maneuvering his way to the top before anyone realizes they were playing his game all along. Alan wrings his hands because they remember. They remember every mission gone wrong, every time he hesitated, every comrade he couldn&apos;t save. His fingers trace scars, phantom pains from injuries long healed, from choices that never will. The war might not have killed him yet, but it&apos;s taken pieces of him - one nervous motion at a time. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Pulls strings from the dark. Never in the spotlight, always in control.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
