			<performanceExamScore>53</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Death isn&apos;t just a consequence of war for Floressa - it&apos;s the objective. She moves through conflict like a reaper, methodical and unrelenting, leaving nothing but silence and ruin in her wake. Floressa customizes everything because she&apos;s seen too many things fail when they shouldn&apos;t. People trust that things will work the way they&apos;re designed. Floressa  knows better. If she built it, if she reinforced it, then at least she knows it won&apos;t fail the moment it&apos;s needed most </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Death is the goal, not the cost. Methodical, unstoppable, thorough.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
