			<personalityDescription>There&apos;s no such thing as overconfidence in Fairuza&apos;s mind. Whether they&apos;re got the skills to back it up or not is irrelevant - they step into every situation like they&apos;ve already won and let reality catch up later. Fairuza doesn&apos;t see convoy missions as boring logistics - they see them as a real test of skill. Protecting a moving force, managing ambush points, bottlenecks, and chokepoints - to them, that&apos;s the real game. &quot;Stationary fights are predictable. Convoy missions? That&apos;s where you prove you know what you&apos;re doing.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Confidence exceeds ability. May succeed through force of will - or get others killed.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
