			<personalityDescription>Alex sees rules as obstacles, not boundaries. If there&apos;s a shortcut to be taken or a loophole to exploit, he&apos;ll find it - ethics and fairness be damned. Alex spends downtime in ways that don&apos;t quite make sense. He maps out old battlefields for fun, builds intricate miniature cities out of plastic building blocks, or memorizes entire books on obsolete military doctrine. No one understands why - and he refuses to explain. </personalityDescription>
