			<performanceExamScore>45</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Violence isn&apos;t just a tool for Salah al Din - it&apos;s the default setting. He sees every interaction as a challenge, every stare as a provocation, and every battle as a chance to break something... or someone. Peace is just the pause before the next conflict. Salah al Din sees every resource as his to claim and his to keep. Whether it&apos;s battlefield salvage or simple supplies, he takes what he can and shares only when absolutely necessary - if at all. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Interprets peace as waiting room for violence. Every glance is a challenge.&lt;br&gt;- Thinks the company&apos;s inventory is theirs. Good luck prying it loose.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
