			<performanceExamScore>55</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>If there&apos;s a bad idea, Berhane will be the first to try it. He hates waiting, hates planning, and definitely hates being told to slow down - because he always believes the best way forward is straight through the enemy. &quot;Being late is the fastest way to get killed.&quot; Berhane drills it into every rookie he meets. In war, seconds matter - hesitate, delay, miss your mark, and you&apos;re dead. His lance jokes that he sets his watch five minutes fast just to make sure he&apos;s never late. They&apos;re only half wrong. It&apos;s ten minutes. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- First to try the worst idea. Hates waiting, planning, and orders.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
