			<performanceExamScore>46</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Jeff doesn&apos;t just win - he makes sure everyone knows he won. He taunts enemies, overplays his hand, and takes flashy risks just for the sake of proving he can. He&apos;s good - he just might not be as good as he thinks. Loyalty is just another tool to be used and discarded. Jeff lies, betrays, and manipulates without hesitation, making promises he never intends to keep. If someone still trusts him, it&apos;s only because they haven&apos;t been burned yet. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Wins loud. Risks big to prove a point - might not be worth it.&lt;br&gt;- Loyalty lasts exactly one paycheck. Maybe less.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
