			<personalityDescription>Wendel&apos;s patience is as short as his temper is explosive. He doesn&apos;t wait, doesn&apos;t deliberate - he reacts, fast and forceful, often leaving those around him scrambling to keep up. Wendel simply doesn&apos;t care. Duties, relationships, and even his own well-being are secondary to whatever he deems important at the moment. If something - or someone - falls apart because of his inattention, that&apos;s their problem, not his. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Zero patience. Reacts fast, hits hard. Team scrambles to keep pace.&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t track gear, doesn&apos;t track people.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
