			<personalityDescription>Subtlety and patience have never been Marinochka&apos;s strengths. They speak before thinking, act before planning, and never apologize for either. If boldness is a virtue, then they consider themself a saint. Marinochka doesn&apos;t just think they&apos;re invincible - they act like it. They take unnecessary risks, dismisses warnings, and underestimate opponents, convinced that sheer skill (or luck) will always pull them through. One day, it won&apos;t. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- No patience, no filter, no regrets. Speaks and acts before thinking. Owns it.&lt;br&gt;- Ignores danger, overestimates skill. One day, luck will run out.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
