			<performanceExamScore>47</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Corina keeps everything - ammo, supplies, spare parts - because you never know when you&apos;ll need them. She refuses to let go of anything useful, even if it means stockpiling more than she could ever realistically use. Corina knows holovids are escapism, but she doesn&apos;t care. They&apos;re structured, predictable, full of meaning. Unlike the mess that is real life, where nothing follows a script and everything falls apart for no reason. &quot;Real life&apos;s got terrible pacing. At least in holovids, things happen for a reason.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Keeps everything that isn&apos;t nailed down. Doesn&apos;t share. Doesn&apos;t trust.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
