			<personalityDescription>Teamwork is just a means to an end for Gina. She&apos;ll play along as long as it benefits her, but the moment there&apos;s something to gain, she won&apos;t hesitate to take more than her fair share. War isn&apos;t personal for Gina - it&apos;s a business. She weighs risks like investments, treats allies like temporary partners, and knows that in the end, survival isn&apos;t about honor - it&apos;s about profit. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Teamwork ends where opportunity begins.&lt;br&gt;- Treats battle like a spreadsheet. Risk/reward to the decimal.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
