			<personalityDescription>For Marie, hesitation is just another form of failure. She throws herself into danger without a second thought, making split-second calls that can mean brilliance or disaster - but either way, she never slows down. While she doesn&apos;t seek attention, Marie notices everything. She listens more than she speaks, analyzes before she acts, and values deep conversations over shallow chatter. Her quiet nature makes her words all the more impactful when she chooses to share them. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Hesitation rejected. Decisions made mid-charge. High risk, high volatility.&lt;br&gt;- Quiet type. Won&apos;t lead the toast, but will notice who&apos;s missing.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
