			<personalityDescription>Lindsay gives because she knows what it&apos;s like to have nothing. She&apos;ll take the hard jobs, give up her share, and put herself in danger for the sake of others - even when it costs her more than she can afford to lose. The company is bleeding resources. The pay is late. Another bunk is empty. Lindsay can&apos;t stop the decline, but she can follow her routines. If the paperwork is done just right, if the tools are placed exactly where they belong, if she does everything in perfect sequence-maybe it&apos;ll feel like things aren&apos;t slipping away. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Gives more than they should. Probably won&apos;t stop until it breaks them.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
