			<personalityDescription>Alemayyehu believes leadership isn&apos;t about consensus - it&apos;s about control. He doesn&apos;t ask for loyalty; he assumes it, and those who resist quickly learn that standing in his way is never a good idea. Alemayyehu will do whatever it takes to survive and profit. He switches sides when the money&apos;s right, abandons allies if the deal goes sour, and never lets sentiment get in the way of a paycheck. If someone wants loyalty, they&apos;d better pay extra. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Loyalty is expected, not earned. Resistance met with swift correction.&lt;br&gt;- Switches sides mid-fight if the payout shifts. Not to be trusted without a signed contract.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
