			<personalityDescription>Godfrey fights for one thing: the highest bidder. They&apos;re not interested in honor, loyalty, or causes - just cold, hard cash and a contract that keeps them alive and well-paid. Godfrey writes names. They write dates. They write everything because they&apos;ve seen too many people vanish without a trace. No records. No burial. Just gone. So they record them, their stories, their moments - because in a war where people disappear overnight, maybe this way, they&apos;ll still exist. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Hired gun. No cause, no loyalty - just money.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
