			<personalityDescription>Benny doesn&apos;t need recognition - he just wants his people to succeed. Whether in battle, in planning, or in moments of doubt, he offers steady, unwavering support that reminds others they&apos;re never truly alone. Benny&apos;s speech patterns are completely unpredictable. One moment, he&apos;s speaking with a crisp, formal tone; the next, he&apos;s dropped into a thick drawl or clipped military jargon. &quot;Aye, lad, ye best watch yer flank - oh, wait, I mean, move your ass before they frag you.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Not in it for glory. Just wants the team to make it home.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
