			<performanceExamScore>49</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Erik&apos;s loyalty is as fleeting as a paycheck. He makes allies when it&apos;s convenient, breaks deals when it suits him, and always keeps an escape route ready in case things turn south. Erik doesn&apos;t keep his special object because it makes him happy. He keeps it because it reminds him of what&apos;s been lost. A tag from a dead comrade, a ring from a life left behind, a torn page from a book he never got to finish. He doesn&apos;t talk about it. He doesn&apos;t need to. Anyone who looks into his eyes when he holds it already understands. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Slippery. Never in the wrong, never where you left them.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
