			<personalityDescription>Most people aren&apos;t worth Orghlaith&apos;s attention - at least, that&apos;s how she sees it. Whether it&apos;s new recruits, subordinates, or anyone beneath her notice, she brushes them aside with a look of boredom and a dismissive wave. Orghlaith doesn&apos;t care about technical readouts or factory settings - she knows when a unit feels right. If she&apos;s forced into something that doesn&apos;t match her, she feels it immediately. &quot;You don&apos;t pick something based on numbers. You feel what belongs to you.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t even look back when leaving someone behind - already onto the next thing.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
