			<personalityDescription>Hank doesn&apos;t deal in half-truths or carefully worded pleasantries. He calls things exactly as he sees them, no matter how uncomfortable it makes people - because, to him, honesty is more valuable than diplomacy. Hank doesn&apos;t lie, even when he probably should. &quot;You&apos;re a terrible shot,&quot; he tells a rookie after a botched drill. &quot;That flank will collapse in three minutes if we don&apos;t move now,&quot; he warns the commander. No one ever likes what he has to say - but ignoring him tends to get people killed. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Says the thing everyone else avoids - loud, clear, and on purpose.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
