			<personalityDescription>Felix wears his confidence like a badge of honor, parading his victories with flair and dismissing setbacks as temporary blips. His unwavering belief in his own prowess often blinds him to potential dangers, even as he dazzles onlookers with his bold, if misguided, bravado. Felix speaks in poetry because it keeps the emptiness at bay. He&apos;s seen too many things that don&apos;t deserve to be remembered - but somehow, words make them bearable. If he stops finding poetry in the world, then all that&apos;s left is the cold, empty void of everything that&apos;s been lost. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Flaunts wins, shrugs off losses. Blind spots hidden behind bravado.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
