			<personalityDescription>Once Montana commits to something, that&apos;s the end of the discussion. No argument, no persuasion, no force in the universe is enough to shake their resolve once they&apos;ve made up their mind. War isn&apos;t personal for Montana - it&apos;s a business. They weigh risks like investments, treat allies like temporary partners, and know that in the end, survival isn&apos;t about honor - it&apos;s about profit. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Discussion ends at commitment. Mind closed, door locked.&lt;br&gt;- Treats battle like a spreadsheet. Risk/reward to the decimal.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
