			<personalityDescription>Heherson is convinced he can handle anything, no matter how big the challenge. He stretches himself thin, takes on risks he shouldn&apos;t, and charges ahead without thinking about whether he can actually pull it off - because failure isn&apos;t part of his vocabulary. Yet. No matter where a conversation starts, Heherson will bring it back to his chosen topic. &quot;Oh, you&apos;re talking about planetary weather patterns? That reminds me of how desert conditions affect &apos;Mek heat sinks!&quot; No one knows how he does it. No one wants him to do it. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Thinks confidence replaces planning. Runs headfirst into collapse.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
