			<personalityDescription>Oleg never stops - because stopping means thinking, and thinking means facing the ghosts that haunt him. He fights, trains, and pushes himself beyond exhaustion, running from a past that never quite lets him rest. Oleg has long since stopped caring about things that don&apos;t directly affect him. Wars rage, people scheme, and alliances crumble - but to him, it&apos;s all just noise. He does what&apos;s necessary and moves on without a second thought. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Pushing past exhaustion to outrun something deeper. Momentum masks pain.&lt;br&gt;- Sees war as noise. Filters everything but orders.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
