			<personalityDescription>Gard moves through life like a ghost, detached from the surrounding chaos. Orders are followed, tasks are completed, but there&apos;s no fire behind their actions - just a quiet acceptance that nothing really changes. Gard&apos;s locker is full of small, seemingly insignificant items - a spent shell casing from their first battle, a scrap of fabric from an old unit patch, a dented dog tag that isn&apos;t their. &quot;They&apos;re just reminders,&quot; they say when asked. Reminders of what, they never say. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Operates on autopilot. Body moves. Mind&apos;s already gone.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
