			<performanceExamScore>49</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>The line between confidence and recklessness is one Louis never bothers to acknowledge. He acts on impulse, ignores warnings, and barrels forward at full speed, trusting that he&apos;ll figure things out before it&apos;s too late. Louis always seems like he&apos;s one bad moment away from snapping. Whether it&apos;s a broken piece of gear, a slow-witted subordinate, or just a long day, his irritation simmers just beneath the surface, waiting for an excuse to boil over. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t care if it&apos;s reckless - just that it&apos;s fast and loud.&lt;br&gt;- Complains the whole op. Still finishes first.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
