			<performanceExamScore>51</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Fear died a long time ago for Wang. They walk through hell with a steady hand, not because they don&apos;t understand the danger, but because they refuse to let it matter. If death comes, Wang will meet it head-on. Wang isn&apos;t checking the time to stay on schedule - they&apos;re counting down. How long until the next battle. How long until reinforcements stop coming. How long until the company finally collapses. They won&apos;t say what they&apos;re waiting for, but the way they stare at their watch... it&apos;s like they already know. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Fear is dead weight. Walks into hell like it&apos;s routine. Faces death eye-to-eye.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
