			<personalityDescription>People want to believe Dhurai, and that&apos;s the danger. He sounds sincere, looks reliable, and acts like he has your back - until the moment it benefits him to do otherwise. Every briefing, every engagement, every conversation - Dhurai is writing. Notes in a datapad, shorthand scribbled on the back of his glove, coordinates scratched into the inside of his bunk. &quot;Memory&apos;s unreliable,&quot; he says, flipping through pages of previous battles. &quot;Records last.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sounds like a friend. Acts like a liability.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
