			<personalityDescription>Faline doesn&apos;t just have confidence - she has certainty. In her mind, she&apos;s always the smartest, strongest, and most capable person around, and anyone who disagrees is simply too blind to see it. Faline tells stories not because they&apos;re entertaining, but because she refuses to let people be forgotten. She speaks of old battles, fallen comrades, places that don&apos;t exist anymore. She remembers so that others won&apos;t have to. Or maybe, because she knows no one else will. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Confidence hardened into certainty. No room for disagreement - only correction.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
