			<personalityDescription>Fear is for the weak, and Eitor has no patience for it. He throws himself into battle with wild abandon, ignoring risks and consequences. Whether it&apos;s bravery or a death wish, sooner or later, it&apos;s going to catch up with him. Eitor is convinced he can handle anything, no matter how big the challenge. He stretches himself thin, takes on risks he shouldn&apos;t, and charges ahead without thinking about whether he can actually pull it off - because failure isn&apos;t part of his vocabulary. Yet. </personalityDescription>
