			<performanceExamScore>49</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Kundam doesn&apos;t just reach for power - he grabs for it, no matter the cost. His ambition drives him to overextend, making enemies and burning bridges as he chases goals that always seem just out of reach. One day, he&apos;ll push too far, and there&apos;ll be no coming back. Kundam doesn&apos;t expect resupplies, doesn&apos;t assume backup is coming. He&apos;s seen what happens when people rely on things they can&apos;t control. If he&apos;s going to survive, it&apos;ll be because he made something out of nothing. &quot;War doesn&apos;t care what you don&apos;t have. You fight with what&apos;s in front of you, or you die waiting for something better.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Ambition outweighs sense. Making enemies faster than allies.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
