			<performanceExamScore>52</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Juan revels in the chaos of battle, seeking out the most brutal engagements with savage glee. He sees enemies not as opponents but as prey, and the battlefield as a hunting ground where only the strong survive. Before every mission, Juan finds a quiet spot, kneels, and draws something into the dirt. If no dirt is available, he scratches it into metal plating or marks it with a grease pen. No one knows what the symbol means, and when asked, he just shrugs. &quot;Keeps me alive,&quot; he says. The lance isn&apos;t sure if he&apos;s joking. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Revels in brutal combat. Hunts, doesn&apos;t fight. Sees enemies as prey.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
