			<personalityDescription>The more dangerous the path, the more certain Ursula is that it&apos;s the right one. They move forward without fear, seeing every unknown as a puzzle to solve, a victory to claim, or a story to tell later. Ursula isn&apos;t interested in quick victories - they&apos;re interested in certain victories. They wait, watch, and maneuver every piece into place before making their move, ensuring that when the moment comes, their enemies never see it coming. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- The harder the path, the more they want it. Danger is proof they&apos;re on track.&lt;br&gt;- Prefers certainty to speed. Strikes only when the board is set.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
