			<personalityDescription>Some call it paranoia; Ofelia calls it survival. She keeps her eyes open, her mind sharp, and her instincts honed, because the moment she lets her guard down, she knows that&apos;s when disaster will strike. Slowing down just isn&apos;t in Ofelia&apos;s nature. She thrives in constant motion, always chasing the next opportunity, the next fight, the next thrill - because standing still is the only thing that truly unsettles her. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 56%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Calls it survival, not paranoia. Guard never drops, not for a second.&lt;br&gt;- Stillness is discomfort. Chases motion like its purpose.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
