			<personalityDescription>Barnabá talks a good game about loyalty and teamwork, but at the end of the day, he&apos;s only loyal to himself. He knows exactly when to walk away, who to throw under the bus, and how to spin things so he always lands on his feet. Barnabá says what he means and means what he says. He doesn&apos;t believe in playing games or sugarcoating the truth - his words and actions come from a place of honesty, making him a rare presence in a world full of deception. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Loyalty ends the moment the benefit does.&lt;br&gt;- Speaks plain. Earns trust the old-fashioned way.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
