			<personalityDescription>Ann always looks out for number one. If a situation doesn&apos;t benefit her directly, she&apos;s not interested. She&apos;ll work with others when it suits her, but the moment it stops being profitable, she&apos;s already moving on. Ann doesn&apos;t like silence. It feels unnatural, wrong, too empty. If no one else is talking, she&apos;ll fill the void, even if it gets her in trouble. &quot;Okay, but hypothetically, if I were to just start humming right now...&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Helps when it helps them - otherwise, not their problem.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
