			<personalityDescription>For Sandra, combat isn&apos;t just a job - it&apos;s a sport, and she is always eager to rack up a higher score. She treats every battle like a game of &quot;who can make the biggest explosion,&quot; cracking jokes over comms while turning enemies into scrap. If war ever ended, Sandra would probably be bored to death. Sandra never stops - because stopping means thinking, and thinking means facing the ghosts that haunt her. She fights, trains, and pushes herself beyond exhaustion, running from a past that never quite lets her rest. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Treats war like sport. Competes for kill count. Jokes over comms.&lt;br&gt;- Pushing past exhaustion to outrun something deeper. Momentum masks pain.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
