			<personalityDescription>Mui-Yin doesn&apos;t believe in second chances or sentimental attachments. If someone can&apos;t keep up, they&apos;re left behind. She sees emotions as liabilities, and nothing - not guilt, grief, or regret - will slow her down. Mui-Yin doesn&apos;t believe in luck or optimism. She&apos;s seen too many brilliant strategies collapse because no one thought about contingencies. She strategizes relentlessly, because in war, the best plans are the ones that don&apos;t get you killed when they fail. </personalityDescription>
