			<personalityDescription>Josh never doubts himself, even when he absolutely should. He struts into battle like he&apos;s already won and dismisses any challenge with a smirk. If someone questions his skills, he&apos;ll be the first to bet his wages on proving them wrong. Most people aren&apos;t worth Josh&apos;s attention - at least, that&apos;s how he sees it. Whether it&apos;s new recruits, subordinates, or anyone beneath his notice, he brushes them aside with a look of boredom and a dismissive wave. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 36%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Never doubts, even when wrong. Swagger first, strategy later.&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t even look back when leaving someone behind - already onto the next thing.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
