			<personalityDescription>Melina doesn&apos;t measure risk the way others do. Where they see danger, she sees duty; where others hesitate, she moves forward. Not because she doesn&apos;t feel fear, but because she refuses to let it define her. Melina believes that strength isn&apos;t just about winning battles - it&apos;s about lifting others up. She offers encouragement when morale is low, steps in when someone struggles, and always ensures those around her feel seen and valued. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees duty, not danger. Fear present - but doesn&apos;t get a say.&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t forget the people in the fight. Makes sure no one gets left behind.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
